a0","name":"Damian","lastName":"Strojny","uuid":"C66D53156D3D3CC9AAA979342952F93F271B26027AE5517F99BF2AC77570F59B36A88CF7505BF7215CE961F62C3D2ABD499FB409C0BEE636A03BFF432E35CA53","documentHash":"53d170c9-63ca-480b-83d1-33683f0405b8"},{"objectId":"5e7093a1878c28a0473ae097","name":"Irena","lastName":"Puszkarz","uuid":"7748E129951830361627A2122A939E97400E0281F87A4514E834E950A465D8B792DEE11574C07936E8568C452C562625273EA0CED4C1FD7D12AAFFA8D56D3EFF","documentHash":"207c364b-b7af-49e4-8f73-4dc05f3908cc"}],"objectId":"68405435fdbe834dc27c36af","publicUri":"http://pmr.edu.pl/2024_xxiv_1-63-_2.html","type":"ARTICLE","typeName":"Artykuł","year":2024,"title":"Realizacja szczepień przeciw HPV w placówkach Podstawowej Opieki Zdrowotnej – szczepienie zalecane","otherTitles":[{"languageCode":"eng","title":"Implementation of HPV vaccinations in Primary Health Care facilities – vaccination recommended"}],"abstracts":[{"languageCode":"pol","content":"W pracy przedstawiono wpływ szczepionek przeciwko HPV na zmniejszenie liczbyprzypadków nowotworów związanych z wirusem brodawczaka HPV. Rocznie w Polsce odnotowuje się około 1,6 tysiąca przypadków zachorowań na nowotwory złośliwe u mężczyzn oraz 4,4 tysiąca u kobiet, które są ściśle związane z obecnością wirusa HPV . Szczepienia ochronne stanowią najważniejszy element strategii profilaktyki, który umożliwia zapobieganie tym chorobom oraz redukując ogólną liczbę zachorowań. Oczekiwane zmiany w zdrowiu publicznym nie nastąpią natychmiastowo. Pierwsze wyraźne spadki zapadalności na raka szyjki macicy będą obserwowane po około 10 latach od wprowadzenia szczepień."},{"languageCode":"eng","content":"The paper presents the impact of HPV vaccines on reducing the number of cancer casesassociated with the HPV papillomavirus. Each year, there are approximately 1.6 thousand cases of malignant tumors in men and 4.4 thousand in women, which are closely related to the presence of the HPV virus in Poland. Vaccinations are the most important element of the prevention strategy, which helps to prevent these diseases and reduces the overall number of illnesses. The expected changes in public health will not occur immediately. The first direct decrease in the incidence of cervical cancer will be observed approximately 10 years after the introduction of vaccinations."}],"affiliations":[{"id":"5e70918b878c28a04737de79","uid":"buOj2HS_oqcB_wF3PzkVTFg","uuid":"a615aecb-b546-472b-93d9-813564c4b50d","name":"Państwowa Akademia Nauk Stosowanych w Przemyślu","affiliatedPersonIDs":["62354e387523402df09433a0","5e7093a1878c28a0473ae097"],"parentId":"5e70918b878c28a04737de79","parentUuid":"a615aecb-b546-472b-93d9-813564c4b50d","rootId":"5e70918b878c28a04737de79","rootUuid":"a615aecb-b546-472b-93d9-813564c4b50d","type":"AUTHOR"}],"mainLanguage":"pol","mainLanguageName":"polski","volume":"XXIV","issue":"1 (63)","pagesFromTo":"8-11","articleEvaluation":{"indexedJournal":false,"isReview":false,"wosConference":false},"contributionOrder":{"AUTHOR":["62354e387523402df09433a0","5e7093a1878c28a0473ae097","68405b98fdbe834dc27c54e9"]},"journal":{"objectId":"5e6f7d52878c28514547a33e","mniswId":"1001682","title":"Problemy Medycyny Rodzinnej","issn":"1507-5222","metadataSource":"IMPORT","documentHash":"9de49fd8-0026-41fd-9d7d-2363b74ae0f7"},"_version":4,"journalIssue":{"objectId":"68404730fdbe834dc27aafad","year":"2024","volume":"XXIV","number":"1 (63)","doi":"","documentHash":"7fa9f2e4-fec8-4ddd-a893-96b8d23b2d43"},"translation":false,"editors":[],"translators":[],"institutionProfile":false,"translationEditors":[],"keywords":[{"languageCode":"pol","keywords":["HPV (human papillomavirus) – ludzki wirus brodawczaka","Narodowy Fundusz Zdrowia","Narodowa Strategia Onkologiczna","podstawowa opieka zdrowotna","program szczepień ochronnych","zakażenie przenoszone drogą płciową"]},{"languageCode":"eng","keywords":["human papillomavirus","National Health Fund","National Oncology Strategy","Primary Health Care","Preventive Vaccination Program","Sexually T